# The table editor, drawing (tests/t1/pinball3d_editor.sh), window 1440x900: paths, arcs, snapping, mirror, a ramp and its height
# profile, the palette, duplicate. An entry of the palette is taken by its key (Cmd+G, "+wall"), a field by its key (Cmd+F): the
# lines of the palette and of the forms may move when the format grows, the top view does not.
# A wall: three points on the table (they snap to the 5 mm grid), Enter.
4 key g meta
5 text +wall
6 key Enter
8 move 567 519
9 down
10 up
11 move 600 486
12 down
13 up
14 move 633 519
15 down
16 up
17 key Enter
# Its middle point is dragged 5 cm up the table.
20 move 600 486
21 down
22 move 600 470
23 move 600 453
24 up
# Its first stretch is bent into an arc with the round dot in its middle.
27 move 584 486
28 down
29 move 575 482
30 move 568 478
31 up
# A double click on its second stretch adds a point there; the last point is pressed, and Delete takes that point away.
34 move 617 486
35 down
36 up
37 down
38 up
41 move 633 519
42 down
43 up
44 key Delete
# M adds its mirror image about the table's axis.
47 key m
# A ramp: two points, and a double click for the last.
50 key g meta
51 text +ramp
52 key Enter
54 move 666 618
55 down
56 up
57 move 666 552
58 down
59 up
60 move 699 519
61 down
62 up
63 down
64 up
# Its height profile, found by its key: the point in the middle is dragged later and lower, and a double click adds a point.
67 key f meta
68 text profile
70 move 1242 189
71 down
72 move 1250 200
73 move 1270 212
74 up
76 move 1340 189
77 down
78 up
79 down
80 up
# A bumper: one click; then its copy (Cmd+D).
83 key g meta
84 text +bumper
85 key Enter
87 move 620 453
88 down
89 up
91 key d meta
# Save.
94 key s meta
